<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Callias of Chalcis</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">4th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Callias of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chalcis">Chalcis</a> was a Euboean politician who in the 340s BCE sought to unite <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euboea">Euboea</a> under the leadership of Chalcis, reviving the Euboean League. He moved between alliances with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-ii-of-macedon">Philip II of Macedon</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a>, and with Athenian help drove out pro-Macedonian tyrants on the island in 341 BCE. He was honoured with Athenian citizenship.</p></div>
